    "text": "To determine how many more rocks Albert collected than Joshua, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the number of rocks Jose collected.\n2. Calculate the number of rocks Albert collected.\n3. Find the difference between the number of rocks Albert collected and the number of rocks Joshua collected.\n\nFirst, we know that Joshua collected 80 rocks. Jose collected 14 fewer rocks than Joshua. Therefore, we can calculate the number of rocks Jose collected as follows:\n\\[\n\\text{Number of rocks Jose collected} = 80 - 14 = 66\n\\]\n\nNext, we know that Albert collected 20 more rocks than Jose. Therefore, we can calculate the number of rocks Albert collected as follows:\n\\[\n\\text{Number of rocks Albert collected} = 66 + 20 = 86\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to find out how many more rocks Albert collected than Joshua. We do this by subtracting the number of rocks Joshua collected from the number of rocks Albert collected:\n\\[\n\\text{Difference} = 86 - 80 = 6\n\\]\n\nThus, Albert collected \\(\\boxed{6}\\) more rocks than Joshua.",
